Add a corner-radius control to the LivePress Design screen.

Applies to **LivePress 1.5.2**, the version installed at admin.auxtechint.com
— not to the 1.0.0 copy sitting next to this file, which is an older snapshot
and does not contain the Design screen this patches. Paths are relative to
wp-content/plugins/livepress/.

WHY
The Design screen shipped four colour controls and no radius, on the reasoning
recorded in its own source: "Radius is gone: there is no radius token to
drive." That was true of the codebase LivePress was first written against.
This frontend has --radius, and src/lib/design-tokens.ts already reads a
`radius` key off the design global — it simply had no UI, so the only way to
set it was to POST the option by hand.

WHAT
- livepress.php: a fifth token, `kind => 'length'`, with min/max/step/unit.
  A token is a colour unless it says otherwise, so the four existing entries
  are untouched.
- assets/editor.js: a `lengthRow()` branch — slider plus number, in px. It
  keeps the colours' rule that a value equal to the brand default is not an
  override and is deleted, so Reset hands the token back to the stylesheet.
  The colour path is not modified.
- assets/editor.css: track widths for the four-control row, and the slider,
  number and unit.

The value is stored bare ("4", not "4px") and the frontend appends the unit,
which is what makes 0 a real setting rather than an empty one.

VERIFIED
`node --check` on the patched editor.js; brace balance unchanged against the
originals; 13 behaviour tests against lengthRow() lifted out of the patched
file (clamping, delete-on-default, 0 stored, empty-box-while-typing ignored,
reset, Reset-all registration, re-render from a saved value). The storage
contract was confirmed live end to end: writing {"radius":"4"} to the design
global rendered `:root{--radius: 4px}` on auxtechint.com and visibly squared
the cards.

INSTALLED 2026-09-22
All three files uploaded and confirmed byte-identical on the server
(sha256 + size), with WordPress healthy afterwards — REST, login and the
Design screen all answering, no fatal. `livepress_asset_version()` is
filemtime-based, so the version string bumped itself and nobody gets a cached
editor.js.

The control was then rendered from the *served* editor.js against the *live*
editor.css and driven in a browser: slider and number stay in step, returning
to the default deletes the override rather than storing 12, 0 is kept, an
out-of-range number clamps on blur, Reset clears. The row lines up with the
colour rows above it. The owner confirmed it appears on the Design screen in
wp-admin, which is the one link a session cannot reach — an application
password does not authenticate wp-admin.

To apply: git apply --directory=<livepress plugin dir> radius-control-1.5.2.patch
or just upload the three patched files.

